+   *
+   * Number of H.264 slices to split each encoded frame into. Slice boundaries
+   * are macroblock-row aligned and the rows are distributed as evenly as
+   * possible across the slices. More slices shrink the blast radius of a lost
+   * packet (a lost packet damages one slice instead of the whole frame), at a
+   * small coding-efficiency cost. The value is clamped at encode time to the
+   * number of macroblock rows and to the driver's
